-- allEVars SCC-EDGE GUARD: a top-level binding whose only reference to a
-- LATER-defined function sits inside a `Map { … }` literal.
--
-- `desugar.lowerContainerLiterals` lowers `Map { … }` to an `EHeadAnnot`-wrapped
-- `fromEntries` call.  `typecheck.allEVars` — the free-variable walk behind
-- `processTopGroups` -> `depGraphMap` -> `depsOf` -> `clauseRefs`, which feeds
-- Tarjan's SCC ordering of top-level bindings — used to end in a `_ => []`
-- catch-all with no `EHeadAnnot` arm.  So `g` got NO dependency edge to `f`,
-- was inferred before it, and check/run/build all rejected the program with
-- `Unbound variable: f`.
--
-- .expected = ACCEPT.  Ground truth for .out was derived by hand from the
-- program (`f 2` = 4, one entry keyed 1) and cross-checked against the
-- forward-order spelling (`f` defined BEFORE `g`), which accepts and prints
-- the same value both before and after the fix — definition ORDER must not
-- change a well-typed program's meaning.
import map.{Map, entries}

g : Map Int Int
g = Map { 1 => f 2 }

f x = x + x

main = println (entries g)
